# PastryMaster Project Documentation

## Introduction

PastryMaster is a bakery-themed educational game created with Java and LibGDX.
The goal of the game is to complete dessert recipes by selecting correct ingredients and decorating cakes.

---

# System Architecture

The project follows an object-oriented modular structure.

Main components:

- Main.java → starts the game
- GameState.java → stores shared global data
- screens package → handles gameplay screens
- assets folder → stores textures and sounds

---

# Main Screens

## MainMenuScreen
Displays the main menu and starts the game.

## ChefSelectScreen
Allows the player to choose a chef character.

## RecipeScreen
Shows the recipe before gameplay starts.

## CookingScreen
Main gameplay mechanics occur here.

## DecorationScreen
Player decorates the final dessert.

## WinScreen
Displays score and level completion.

---

# Audio System

The game contains:
- background music
- click sounds
- success/error effects

All sounds are loaded inside GameState.

---

# Design Patterns

## Facade Pattern
Used in Main.java for simplified game startup.

## Factory Method
Used for creating ingredients and decorations dynamically.

## State Pattern
Used for level progression and gameplay state handling.

## Template Method
Used through Screen lifecycle methods.

## Observer Pattern
Used through ClickListener and UI events.

---

# Gameplay Mechanics

- Drag-and-drop ingredient selection
- Timer-based recipe memorization
- Multiple recipe levels
- Heart/life system
- Decoration mechanics

